## Real-Time UI State Synchronization & Instant Upgrade Reflections

When an administrator upgrades a plan, all active team members viewing the dashboard experience an instant UI transition from 'Free Plan' to 'Enterprise Tier' without reloading the web page, backed by automatic reactive store updates.

---

## Handling Complex Subscription Lifecycles & Proration Logics

Managing seat modifications mid-cycle requires computing tier difference prorations via Stripe's Billing API. Webhooks capture `invoice.incoming` events to present accurate billing previews before users confirm seat increases.

---

## Client-Side WebSocket Reconnection & Offline Queue Management

Mobile clients and spotty connections require robust reconnection handlers. Buffering pending UI operations in IndexedDB while socket connections are degraded guarantees user intent is preserved when network connectivity returns.

```typescript
import { io } from "socket.io-client";

const socket = io(import.meta.env.VITE_WS_URL, {
  autoConnect: true,
  reconnectionAttempts: 10,
  reconnectionDelay: 1000,
  reconnectionDelayMax: 5000,
});

socket.on("connect", () => {
  console.log("[WS Client] Connected to real-time billing channel");
});

socket.on("subscription:updated", (payload) => {
  // Update state management store (e.g., Zustand / Pinia)
  useBillingStore.getState().updatePlan(payload);
});
```

---

## Rate Limiting Webhook Endpoints & DDoS Protection Strategies

Exposing public webhook endpoints demands protective rate limiting. Deploying Cloudflare rules and Nginx rate-limiting zones prevents flood attacks while whitelisting Stripe's official IP range prefixes.
